        "Actions:\n- Define the ideal customer profile.\n- Identify the customer's desired outcome.\n- Standardise the core offer.\n- Define packages and optional add-ons.\n- Set minimum margin and approval rules.\n- Build a quote calculator.\n- Define scope and change-order rules.\n- Review payment terms and deposit requirements.\nDeliverables:\n- Offer document.\n- Pricing calculator.\n- Quote template.\n- Scope and change-control policy.\n- Payment schedule.\nDays 31–45: Improve the sales process\nObjective: make conversion less dependent on improvisation.",
        "Actions:\n- Audit successful and unsuccessful sales conversations.\n- Identify what the founder does differently.\n- Write the sales process.\n- Build a discovery-call structure.\n- Create pre-call and decision-maker assets.\n- Create an objection FAQ.\n- Train the team through role-play.\n- Introduce daily coaching and pipeline reviews.\nDeliverables:\n- Sales playbook.\n- Call and message examples.\n- Sales assets.\n- Team coaching schedule.\n- CRM stage definitions.\nDays 46–60: Scale the strongest acquisition channel\nObjective: increase qualified demand through a proven route.",
        "Actions:\n- Compare channels by customer quality and contribution.\n- Choose the strongest existing channel.\n- Improve prospect research.\n- Improve outreach personalisation.\n- Set a sustainable activity target.\n- Train the team on the proven process.\n- Track channel-level results.\n- Avoid adding unrelated channels during the test.\nDeliverables:\n- Acquisition channel scorecard.\n- Prospect list criteria.\n- Outreach workflow.\n- Weekly channel performance report.\nDays 61–75: Build partnerships and repeat-business opportunities\nObjective: access more qualified customers and improve customer lifetime value.",
        "Actions:\n- Identify relevant associations and industry events.\n- Evaluate sponsorship and speaking opportunities.\n- Create a useful event resource or presentation.\n- Build a consent-based lead capture process.\n- Create a post-project review.\n- Identify repeat-purchase cycles.\n- Test a multi-project offer where appropriate.\nDeliverables:\n- Event and partnership shortlist.\n- Event ROI model.\n- Follow-up workflow.\n- Repeat-business offer.\nDays 76–90: Review, narrow, and systematise\nObjective: double down on what is producing profitable growth.",
